nited States Army general during World War II?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"George S. Patton led the Third Army after the Normandy invasion, and his forces helped liberate much of France.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7e76-b700-793fa7717d0c","description":"George S. Patton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-77d6-8d74-ab264cb0855a","description":"David Dixon Porter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7484-9a9e-edabfa4838d3","description":"George Elliot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-728a-8cdd-243d0bb28cab","description":"Philip Sheridan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-784b-9ea2-f9e39ac24064","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the American Civil War end?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Civil War ended in 1865; Lee\'s surrender at Appomattox Court House in April marked a decisive turning point, though fighting continued briefly elsewhere.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-714b-8978-174ada2e245e","description":"1865","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7d8b-a950-29c2606d3510","description":"1863","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76a2-a738-d99d9287717a","description":"1861","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ca0-a7bc-82471091799c","description":"1877","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7175-ab2e-45ccd0ceb7bb","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Betrayed by a fellow gang member, which Wild West outlaw was shot dead in 1882 while dusting a picture frame?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Jesse James was already a notorious post-Civil War outlaw when Robert Ford shot him, hoping to collect a reward.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-77d8-b6c8-59934c66e75b","description":"Jesse James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a22-88a1-506805e726e0","description":"Billy the Kid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7673-ab7b-eea461f3843b","description":"Butch Cassidy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-70e1-9843-28349cc5d882","description":"John Wesley Hardin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a14-98f9-95227b138918","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the European Union (EU) form?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Maastricht Treaty was signed in 1992 and brought the European Union into existence when it took effect the following year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7db4-8c7f-206b4e5a9d38","description":"1993","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ee8-ab54-c7edf7041371","description":"1973","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-719e-a845-03526b1c0fe5","description":"1953","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7afa-9dbd-b95c3f655c57","description":"1933","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-79d5-b8e5-a55286d4b8a7","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"As what is the Frankish ruler Charles the Great better known?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Charlemagne united much of western and central Europe, and his reign helped foster the Carolingian Renaissance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7057-9a01-c9bf56cfd2ba","description":"Charlemagne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7379-b603-98a5f1c92304","description":"Charles the Bald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-70e2-87bd-3ed7682f8fe8","description":"Charlione","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7dea-9afd-fdbfd4527e60","description":"Charity Charles","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-741d-b54a-4ec388e3d9b4","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What explorer landed in China and reached Kublai Khan\'s court in 1275?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Marco Polo\'s travels, reaching Kublai Khan\'s court around 1275, were recorded in The Travels of Marco Polo.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7f5d-9163-13b22e5f9fe1","description":"Marco Polo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-766b-a4dc-de236482