","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-739c-a6e5-3d7413783eab","description":"Harold Wilson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-79a1-834f-79f58a266829","description":"Tony Blair","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7270-b63d-f67719ec92d5","description":"John Major","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-781e-9ac8-e3888d6f4848","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which US election year were the supporters of the Democratic candidate paraphrasing the popular song \"Hello Dolly\" to \"Hello Lyndon\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In 1964, Lyndon B. Johnson won a full term after succeeding Kennedy, defeating Republican Barry Goldwater in a landslide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ef3-bbe0-e7783cea18b2","description":"1964","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-71b9-9c5d-d893f68f4eb3","description":"1944","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76cd-a6e3-2497738edf15","description":"1980","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7178-918b-df2cb0725aad","description":"1992","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76bd-90f8-cf1158f6db01","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the monarch of The United Kingdom during the time period 1837-1901?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Victoria was the first British monarch to make Buckingham Palace her official residence.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-78d6-8d34-a327ff2d873f","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7bf8-b570-34fd765b8260","description":"Mary II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76f1-9855-222c5b73bc50","description":"Richard I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-72ed-8193-a088be3f2f5e","description":"William IV","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7f14-aad7-6bd6d20d1df9","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Church body, set up in the 13th century to root out heresy, became known for its trials and torture?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The medieval Inquisition was a series of church tribunals. The Spanish Inquisition, established later, became especially notorious, though it was a distinct institution.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a15-9a91-d1de439ddd13","description":"The Inquisition","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7c7d-87d1-5766d2e45133","description":"The Knights Templar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ea1-a892-4eb25c9071a4","description":"The Curia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7cdf-a370-145feec68081","description":"The Jesuits","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7589-8999-7200a88a5e7a","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The eldest sons of the kings of which country held the title \'Dauphin\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The title came from the Dauphin\u00e9, a region that became part of the royal domain; it was later used for the heir to the French throne.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7172-8bbe-1ca7af0ec52c","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7961-8c07-f8764567b615","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-75a1-acc0-548ac5e18f5e","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7bf8-bbe8-92ed3dd959b2","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-78ff-95d2-116d6a34acc1","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Founded in 1636, what is the oldest university in the USA?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Harvard was named for John Harvard, a clergyman whose bequest of books and money helped the young college grow.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a21-895e-f433c12730c7","description":"Harvard","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7950-8520-83338a446f61","description":"Stanford","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-70cc-9d88-1b94e90be95b","description":"Cornell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7244-b5a4-88