ipher Egyptian hieroglyphs.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7104-832c-fb00365b18c5","description":"The Rosetta Stone","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-73d7-91e5-8eb5e6d6c762","description":"The Philosopher\'s Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7d1e-a459-d9ac996597d1","description":"The Stone of Destiny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7530-b377-0a31a27f7ddf","description":"The Cornerstone","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-720e-85e5-4c317e847c7c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which British general commanded the army that surrendered at Yorktown in the American Revolution?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"American and French forces surrounded Charles Cornwallis at Yorktown, while the French navy blocked British relief, forcing his surrender.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7bd8-bc02-5bc67fa1f3a9","description":"Charles Cornwallis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7280-bf11-8349a35c4d77","description":"John Burgoyne","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a85-a926-dba2cbc0f4b4","description":"William Howe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7102-872a-88328fb0e40e","description":"Henry Clinton","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7b54-9e6d-7217e6943aac","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese emperor was buried with an army of thousands of life-sized clay soldiers?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Qin Shi Huang unified China and founded the Qin dynasty. His burial complex includes the terracotta army, intended to guard him in the afterlife.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7b91-9d6d-7d7106303708","description":"Qin Shi Huang","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7aa2-b293-0d8bab427b10","description":"Han Wudi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-71a5-9eb1-78b4b69fa5db","description":"Kangxi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7abd-b03f-07666761f52d","description":"Yongle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ae2-9e05-c54d665e3fe5","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Battles known as Con Thien and Hamburger Hill were fought during which 20th century conflict?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Vietnam refers to the Vietnam War, in which the United States fought alongside South Vietnam against North Vietnam and its allies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7cd4-ad8b-324b9c7011e8","description":"Vietnam","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7ad6-9334-1c373c62f441","description":"Iraq","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7c1f-b1b7-ff7237ba1ffe","description":"Korea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7932-b2fd-4622164b69a6","description":"Afghanistan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-706c-9490-76d0e9019013","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did Neil Armstrong first step onto the Moon?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Armstrong stepped onto the lunar surface after the Apollo 11 spacecraft Eagle landed; Buzz Aldrin followed him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a8b-85bf-d5426c692d9b","description":"1969","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7924-9a07-640433ae0ada","description":"1967","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-77e1-9c23-643b6c68ef4a","description":"1971","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7191-a4a4-fb5e601a209e","description":"1973","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7773-a3f8-69937b982dd1","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year was Hong Kong Island formally ceded to Britain under the Treaty of Nanking?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Britain occupied the island in 1841, and it was ceded by the Treaty of Nanking signed in 1842 after the First Opium War.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7d2c-9419-4500eac10c03","description":"1842","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7b6a-b9bc-66395375c37e","description":"1815","correct_answe