ion":"What fabled city was German adventurer Philipp Von Hutten searching for when he explored South America in the 1540s?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"El Dorado began as a legend about a gold-covered ruler; over time, the story grew into a fabled city or kingdom of riches.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7f42-8246-d3c95cb310aa","description":"El Dorado","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-73a9-b1f5-ba35dd7c42d2","description":"Atlantis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-71bb-81c4-07e9547ea5ce","description":"Shangri-La","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7aa0-bbbd-9da3d7c89b32","description":"Camelot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-75c4-91c8-3792db72e004","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What came to an end in the United States in December 1933?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The 21st Amendment repealed the 18th Amendment, ending Prohibition. It remains the only constitutional amendment to repeal another.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7cc4-a836-f2a90540cf62","description":"Prohibition","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-77d0-904a-e78426b60346","description":"Segregation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-735d-8415-68b4d0a606a7","description":"Slavery","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7948-bca9-7026881581ac","description":"British Rule","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-77f1-8fc5-3bd3b39f939d","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English queen was known as \'The Virgin Queen\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Elizabeth I never married, and her reign is often called the Elizabethan era, known for the flourishing of English theater and exploration.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-71bd-903f-c96015cf48dc","description":"Elizabeth I","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7552-9265-cf9f7bdaf897","description":"Mary I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7486-b37c-fb0d07b06430","description":"Anne Boleyn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7da4-89a9-134ed1ae25be","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-781d-82a0-cbe55469b04e","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What Russian city was known as Leningrad between 1924 and 1991?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"St Petersburg was renamed Petrograd in 1914 and Leningrad in 1924; the city restored its original name in 1991.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-72a8-9846-79830a15949f","description":"St Petersburg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-741b-ac59-99e20ac8ff01","description":"Kazan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7452-be6e-bd198fdd470a","description":"Nizhny Novgorod","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-787b-a790-cde92d204620","description":"Moscow","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-737a-9a25-aaf6d3e58c54","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What ancient civilization occupied the city of Cusco?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Inca made Cusco the capital of their empire, which extended across much of the Andes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-705c-afc4-2d1d40907f05","description":"The Inca","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7c3a-9711-51e5cdae9603","description":"The Aztecs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76c9-94f3-b6fc2aee5078","description":"The Mayans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76f6-bd06-911a48b5ee1c","description":"The Zapotecs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7997-af4c-fc728bdbd181","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What were the first names of US presidents Madison, Monroe, Polk, and Garfield?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"James Madison and James Monroe served as consecutive presidents, with Monroe following Madison.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-760f-bc8b-4497751de4c2","description":"James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-72fa-b758-944b48fb89be"