bel Peace Prize?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Henry Kissinger shared the prize with North Vietnamese diplomat Le Duc Tho for their work on the Vietnam cease-fire; Le Duc Tho declined it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7372-a9ff-51fdd4adfdb5","description":"Henry Kissinger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7f45-8476-47e9428b8ef2","description":"Dean Rusk","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-74c1-85c8-ad66bafc491e","description":"Cyrus Vance","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7f3a-b1ec-ec5851285f84","description":"Madeleine Albright","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7a97-a236-7dc0dec917ac","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"During World War 2, which country was home to the White Rose, a group of student rebels fighting against fascism?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Germany\'s White Rose resistance was centered at the University of Munich; siblings Hans and Sophie Scholl were among its best-known members.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7caf-835c-a724e95a3258","description":"Germany","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-79ad-bca9-f03e00006fdc","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-78e1-8b1c-2a7615620538","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7537-97e2-ebfb0207f762","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-7501-8d49-37c87123cc0b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Leading to the American War of Independence, what was the incident in which tea was dumped into a harbor?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Boston Tea Party was a protest against British taxation, with colonists boarding ships and throwing tea into the harbor.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-76df-a833-291c67c41e7f","description":"Boston Tea Party","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-779e-b32d-a79806e1a6b4","description":"Philadelphia Tea Mutiny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5d-