illes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7cb8-8a35-6038d789f621","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What is the Roman numeral for fifty?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"L represents 50; XL is 40 and LX is 60, using subtraction and addition around it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7e11-b4fd-27aaa719e4d8","description":"L","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-76ed-90fb-9a88c282ad17","description":"R","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7655-b979-666c3010c129","description":"H","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-72e0-9ef6-8a9b34bfdfef","description":"J","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d2e-9019-9da3adbec37b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What type of people were obsessed with turning ordinary metals into gold in the Middle Ages?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alchemists pursued the philosopher\u2019s stone, and some also believed it could help create an elixir of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-72c9-bb50-12c84a29e6aa","description":"Alchemists","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7511-9811-7296ddcdfc58","description":"Hussars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-762c-af3b-0207750b203a","description":"Chandlers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-732a-9e57-e2f5026f7a27","description":"Smelters","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7600-9615-a5badd62c4b1","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Chinese dynasty sent the envoy Zhang Qian west to Central Asia around 138 BC?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Han dynasty sent Zhang Qian during Emperor Wu\u2019s reign. His reports and contacts helped spur trade along routes later known as the Silk Road.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7100-bf61-567e83cb7327","description":"Han dynasty","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-751a-b286-d53e12d0d331","description":"Tang dynasty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7