ans","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-759d-9ec4-43db8cc178fd","description":"Reims","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-72ae-ae4d-2210bb6bdf52","description":"Rouen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7ffa-bb96-e9dffd7df8fe","description":"Paris","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f45-9753-ed0ba7677335","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Before becoming a politician, which US President was a Hollywood actor?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ronald Reagan later served as president of the Screen Actors Guild before entering politics.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7bf2-9f52-12910df785d5","description":"Ronald Reagan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7dc6-b5b4-7135f2e31b59","description":"John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7534-8f72-13cc4a2c7668","description":"Abraham Lincoln","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-74ca-9465-8ab8a521f41a","description":"Barack Obama","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7813-89f2-e873ba7b1b5b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Cold War between the U.S. and Soviet Union begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1947 is often used as the starting point because the Truman Doctrine formalized U.S. opposition to the spread of communism, though the Cold War developed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c74-a75b-15b6577a9c70","description":"1947","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-722a-a9ad-eb3a27faceeb","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-782c-9285-885452f674a4","description":"1938","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d8b-8081-a262e677799a","description":"1955","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-71c9-8477-3b2b01c9d5f1","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the last president of the Soviet Union?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mikhail Gorbachev was the Soviet Union\u2019s first and only president; the office ended when the country dissolved in 1991.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f1e-9a8e-cd1cc604965b","description":"Gorbachev","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7edc-b9a3-27cba7581402","description":"Yeltsin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c4b-88b9-d1398d714158","description":"Putin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7b4e-bf59-277a117c0231","description":"Khrushchev","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7752-9144-3e42c542551d","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who wrote a famous diary between 1660 and 1669?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Samuel Pepys wrote much of his diary in shorthand, and it was not fully published until long after his death.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-705f-bb60-5a630731789a","description":"Samuel Pepys","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-71b5-b807-b65efe4337e3","description":"Anne Frank","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-79c4-acd9-2e6701000cb8","description":"Samuel Johnson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d08-a24e-705cff8db788","description":"Daniel Defoe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7855-ad44-618d4d2db3e4","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the name of the prominent religious conflict that arose in Europe in the 17th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Thirty Years\' War ended with the Peace of Westphalia in 1648, a settlement that reshaped the political map of Central Europe.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-75c9-8904-8a3727ea54f4","description":"The Thirty Years\' War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7af2-ac6a-e0d3620aeb40","description":"The Hundred Years\' War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c71-b5ef-ff3493894557","description":"The War of the Roses","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-73ba-a232-5eec5b613ceb","description":"The War of Spanish Succession","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7219-a157-e6e0ac3bb9e1","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Germany\'s allies in World War I were Austria-Hungary, Bulgaria and which other state?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Ottoman Empire joined the Central Powers in 1914 and fought Allied forces at Gallipoli and across the Middle East.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7dc5-b07c-f51064035a87","description":"The Ottoman Empire","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7fda-ad3d-5f297fd5bf87","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d7a-a909-31706628fb92","description":"Russia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7103-9347-fe0427182269","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7e0c-a3b5-b05dfb7b0a94","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What war was the USA involved in between 1950 and 1953?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Korean War ended in an armistice in 1953, not a formal peace treaty, so the peninsula remains divided.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7ea2-9203-f2c4b90f9b19","description":"Korean War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a08-8a10-afb50ce722b9","description":"Vietnam War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7511-9b19-ee2547e1864f","description":"World War I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-76c9-9f96-50c566312634","description":"World War II","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7be5-8d31-ec6eca5228e6","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the nickname given to the possible computer bug that caused worldwide concern leading up to the year 2000?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Y2K concerns centered on whether software using two-digit years would treat \u201c00\u201d as 1900 instead of 2000, potentially disrupting computer systems.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f0c-a8c1-825918f9dbf3","description":"Y2K","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a32-8727-f0bc1b09637c","description":"Bug2000","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-77b3-8667-64871cb20644","description":"Trojan Horse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7b3a-b72f-0a5163ba1190","description":"The Millennial Worm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-75da-9ba6-de4d11ed3038","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which country was Adolf Hitler born?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Adolf Hitler was born in Braunau am Inn, Austria, in 1889, when the country was part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7dec-ba4d-acd1325c6700","description":"Austria","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7559-8134-8812b627bfc5","description":"Germany","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7856-ba58-ba4ef039b7bb","description":"Belgium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7cca-bb22-658b4882f05d","description":"Switzerland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a4c-8c78-9efe39acccc5","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which French king was married to Marie Antoinette?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Louis XVI was executed by guillotine in 1793; Marie Antoinette was executed later that year.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a28-9336-0f12484f44e0","description":"Louis XVI","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f70-a64b-affd2e9c1392","description":"Louis XIV","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d37-aab4-2755c0c41250","description":"Louis XV","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-727e-9a57-e8e8ea9f1690","description":"Henry IV","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-78a3-a345-15fbe3ddb309","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The 15th century was characterized by a decline in which economic system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Feudalism weakened in parts of Europe as commerce, towns, and stronger monarchies eroded local lords\u2019 power; the pace varied by region.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7246-9240-56f43f978ccf","description":"Feudalism","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a46-b75f-122f0a557a17","description":"Capitalism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-749b-890f-312b255f99ce","description":"Socialism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7410-a12a-754ffa7fbec9","description":"Communism","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f80-aff2-3a438928d6dc","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What is the name given to the period of European history prior to the Renaissance?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Middle Ages is a broad label for the centuries between antiquity and the Renaissance; \u201cDark Ages\u201d is sometimes used for an earlier part of this period, but is less precise.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-723d-a6ef-0d56dc81cc43","description":"Middle Ages","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7026-8c88-ee3a6948bdb5","description":"Classical Period","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f3b-874e-b581bb0b0d7d","description":"Dark Ages","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7e17-864d-367f405b33f3","description":"Age of Exploration","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a9c-8952-0a1756a9281c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"King Ancus Marcius is said to have built the Sublician Bridge, the first bridge across which river in the 7th century B.C.?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Tiber runs through Rome, and the Sublician Bridge became famous in Roman legend for Horatius Cocles\'s stand against an invading army.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-72fb-a6d2-72ddbf1c8f96","description":"The Tiber","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-756a-9f2b-56a1260046c1","description":"The Nile","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7ae4-8cf7-3bfb4df8cb49","description":"The Thames","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7094-849e-a6b1ab139d46","description":"The Seine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d64-8455-ed1f437ebdc9","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What year did World War II begin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"1939 is the year Germany invaded Poland on September 1; Britain and France declared war two days later.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7018-b330-83cce34d382a","description":"1939","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7759-a7ba-80a54f378c0e","description":"1941","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7134-8f61-9f5be5f6ecbb","description":"1945","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-753d-b3de-638447e17fc4","description":"1937","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-72c0-9833-19a8bbfb6a05","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which World War I battle is remembered for the Parisian taxicabs that ferried French troops to the front line in 1914?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The French victory at the Marne halted the German advance toward Paris and helped set the Western Front into a prolonged stalemate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c09-a896-e66f5c93aea4","description":"Battle of the Marne","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-78d3-b568-7fc53a0ab5a7","description":"Battle of the Somme","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d97-b757-dbeddff1ab6a","description":"Battle of Ypres","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7742-8df9-e255303eee82","description":"Battle of Verdun","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7373-890d-b1127b9dad89","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the major economic revolution that started in the 18th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain and reshaped manufacturing as production shifted toward machinery and factories.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a7c-8efa-44297124c767","description":"The Industrial Revolution","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-76d3-9710-1169b0182882","description":"The French Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-736c-a33f-0aaf9f084a3f","description":"The American Revolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7faf-8a4a-5146b1ffcef7","description":"The Enlightenment","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-727d-ba67-396ab7a1c278","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What group of ships, commanded by the Duke of Medina, was considered invincible but was defeated by The Royal Navy in 1588?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Spanish Armada was disrupted by English fireships, and storms battered many ships as they retreated around Scotland and Ireland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7987-a1db-423d1e2d04ea","description":"Spanish Armada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-75eb-9bf4-3e4b66fb50ce","description":"The Napoleonic Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-77ee-b55e-a479b173e804","description":"The Viking Fleet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-75bc-b175-485c68a2116c","description":"The Scottish Armada","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-787b-8b2f-1217e6146376","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the second man to walk on the Moon, after Neil Armstrong?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Buzz Aldrin and Neil Armstrong landed together while Michael Collins remained aboard the command module in lunar orbit.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a42-a27d-4a8ccc898b1e","description":"Buzz Aldrin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-707c-8c30-9492295e5d80","description":"Yuri Gagarin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-70bd-bf48-1da09261dbff","description":"Alan Shepard","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7880-bfd8-f722cce4eca2","description":"James Irwin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7b9f-92ff-0961f54d7a7b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What kind of government dominated most of Europe during the 17th century?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Absolute monarchs centralized authority over government, taxation, and the military. Louis XIV of France is one of the best-known examples.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-74fc-a7a7-e046e55c2ba3","description":"Absolute Monarchy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-78db-931b-64b9053861fb","description":"Democracy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7a30-949c-8443c8695556","description":"Constitutional Monarchy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-76f6-a3e4-e5461af83878","description":"Parliamentary Democracy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f69-9d0e-7d1c2b153f51","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What city was destroyed by a \'little boy\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hiroshima was struck by the first atomic bomb used in warfare, dropped by the U.S. B-29 Enola Gay in August 1945.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7bde-9e79-e3063be5333e","description":"Hiroshima","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c29-b9d7-db66894774d0","description":"Jericho","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7f0a-988d-d8166c65a140","description":"Babel","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7150-b1e5-fd7bd7e11adf","description":"Dresden","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-743c-b036-2d27ab3c9216","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What age preceded the Iron Age?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, and its widespread use gave this period its name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7172-8538-f89217fbe99f","description":"The Bronze Age","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d43-a318-8c75353b656f","description":"The Stone Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7928-95ee-a3366d7bb046","description":"The Steel Age","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7829-8735-4e1b8c5fe1ca","description":"The Wooden Age","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7047-9f46-8b6ec1139979","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What notorious event occurred on the 24th October 1929?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Wall Street Crash began with Black Thursday, as investors rushed to sell shares. The market turmoil helped usher in the Great Depression.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-739b-8ca9-824d5ee228f2","description":"The Wall Street Crash","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7515-a9a0-a83e86abff45","description":"The Hindenberg Disaster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7b9c-af9b-36e68648bbb6","description":"The Assassination of John F. Kennedy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7281-83bb-8713471a379a","description":"The Nazi Invasion of Poland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7587-bdc6-ce265bab4c53","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1945, which German city hosted the trials where former Nazi leaders were prosecuted for war crimes?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The proceedings became known as the Nuremberg Trials and helped establish that political and military leaders could be held individually responsible for international crimes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7437-9fa6-071be4b3e3aa","description":"Nuremberg","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-749e-ba18-5606c95a4525","description":"Berlin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-758a-a659-1a3b835365df","description":"Munich","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-77a5-853f-c6a60df60d08","description":"Frankfurt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-71c3-b8b6-74a2e49d2938","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the term used for a pirate who was licensed by the crown to capture enemy ships and cargo?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A privateer operated under a letter of marque, making attacks on enemy vessels lawful for the crown; pirates acted without that authorization.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-a