":2,"explanation":"Harald Hardrada was killed at Stamford Bridge, a defeat often seen as marking the end of the Viking Age.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7870-836b-f8c627a1abcf","description":"Harald Hardrada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7982-a5dd-a7ca64f26184","description":"Ragnar Lothbrok","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-73e9-9af8-b8dd86ef6147","description":"Ivar the Boneless","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7624-ba0f-baf3f623043a","description":"Sweyn Forkbeard","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7c70-a441-7aa323c4103e","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which American showman founded a circus billed as \'The Greatest Show on Earth\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"P. T. Barnum\'s name later became part of the Barnum & Bailey Circus after he joined forces with James Bailey.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7574-b715-3f3b6c707b39","description":"P. T. Barnum","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-747f-b038-2041183fd50b","description":"Buffalo Bill Cody","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7e92-a8fe-0dd20c9a9092","description":"John Ringling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-783c-86a9-bcff25af6c7d","description":"Harry Houdini","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-77df-be6e-6ffa5c92c057","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The titles Czar and Kaiser both come from the name of which Roman?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Julius Caesar\'s name became a title for rulers, developing into czar in Russian and Kaiser in German.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7636-b4f4-9e9a4dda9907","description":"Julius Caesar","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-729c-94b4-5880f66d1eae","description":"Augustus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-7d4b-a2fa-c74100f823e6","description":"Nero","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae5e-747b-9763-d71f9c6d021c","description":"Constantine","correct_answer":false}]